menu "SK board diagnostics"
    config SK_LOCK_OUTPUT_VERIFIED
        bool "Enable lock output ONLY after electrical corrections and bench checks"
        default n
        help
            The supplied V1.0 schematic connects GPIO3 directly to a PMOS
            gate pulled up to VBAT and shows no coil flyback protection.
            Keep disabled on the unchanged board. First provide a 3.3V-safe
            gate driver, defined OFF during reset/power loss, and appropriate
            inductive suppression. Validate with a dummy load and scope.
    config SK_LOCK_ACTIVE_LOW
        bool "Corrected lock driver is active LOW"
        depends on SK_LOCK_OUTPUT_VERIFIED
        default y
        help
            Match the corrected interface. An NPN driving the PMOS gate
            usually makes the MCU signal active HIGH; disable in that case.
    config SK_POWER_HOLD_PUSH_PULL
        bool "Q1 base series resistor has been fitted: use push-pull hold"
        default n
        help
            V1.0 connects GPIO1 straight to Q1 base. Default uses open-drain
            release with internal pull-up to limit base current. Its ability
            to retain power needs measurement. Enable only with a proper
            external base series resistor.
endmenu
